# Local-dev-backend Compose environment (docker-compose.dev.yml at the repo root).
# Copy to `.env.dev` (gitignored) and `.env.dev.secrets.example` to `.env.dev.secrets`.
# The development templates use working non-production defaults (the private production
# stack's placeholders are not shipped in this repo). AMC
# traffic is fixture-only by default (`AMC_LIVE_FETCH` below); this file is never used in
# CI or production. If you're running more than one instance of this stack on the same
# machine — see `docker-compose.dev.yml`'s header comment and `dev/README.md` for the
# coexistence rules, especially before ever setting `AMC_LIVE_FETCH=true`.
# See `dev/README.md` for how to bring each mode up and what each mode can/can't do.

# ---- Postgres / Valkey ----
# api role, relay role, sweeper role, fetch-worker: all read the same Postgres/broker
# addresses (Compose service names `postgres`/`valkey`). REDIS_URL now must carry the
# Valkey password (ACL auth is required, matching prod's render-acl.sh pattern) — it lives
# in `.env.dev.secrets`/`.env.dev.secrets.example`, not here.
# Non-secret replication role name consumed by docker/postgres/13-scheduler-roles.sh at
# first init (its password lives in `.env.dev.secrets`). Dev-only placeholder, not a
# real credential — the dev stack still connects over the shared DATABASE_URL in
# `.env.dev.secrets`, it only needs the role to exist for migration 022's GRANTs.
POSTGRES_REPLICATION_USER=dev_replicator

# ---- Observability ----
# Dev-only endpoint for local OTel Collector (docker-compose.observability.yml).
# Leave unset to disable telemetry export.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4318
# Namespace dev telemetry so it doesn't mix with prod data in the shared observability stack.
OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES=deployment.environment.name=dev

# ---- api role (apps/server/src/app-config.ts) ----
API_PORT=4000
APP_PG_POOL_MAX=5
APP_PG_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
APP_PG_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
# Dev-only secrets are in `.env.dev.secrets`; never reuse them outside a local throwaway
# Postgres/Valkey.
# No real relay hop in dev (the api container is reached directly on the published port),
# so this has no real "trusted peer" to name — 127.0.0.1/32 is a functionally-inert value,
# not a security-relevant choice here.
RELAY_PEER_CIDR=127.0.0.1/32
# ADR 0006 §A.1's showtimes freshness ceiling (10 min) — generous on purpose, so a seeded
# dev session doesn't need re-seeding mid-session (real value, not a dev invention).
FRESHNESS_MS=600000
RETRY_AFTER_SECONDS=5
STREAM_BLOCK_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
# ADR 0006 §A.2's recheck deadline (real value, not a dev invention).
RECHECK_DEADLINE_MS=30000
# ADR 0024 amendment's pinned W (real value, not a dev invention).
RECHECK_RECOVERY_ROW_WEIGHT=2
# Relative to the api role's WORKDIR (/app/apps/server in the built image) — the already-
# committed synthetic ASN fixture, safe to use as a real value (not test-only despite its
# location: it is a synthetic table, not real MaxMind data, so shipping it as a working dev
# default carries no license/data concern).
ASN_DATABASE_PATH=test/support/fixtures/geolite2-asn-synthetic.csv
# Structured config — same JSON-in-env convention the server documents in
# `apps/server/src/app-config.ts`: SEARCH_LIMITS_JSON is the real @seatfirst/core DEFAULT_SEARCH_LIMITS shipped default, not a dev invention.
SEARCH_LIMITS_JSON={"maxDateSpanDays":30,"maxResolvedShowtimes":200,"maxPartySize":6,"maxTheatres":25,"areaSelectorEnabled":true,"maxAreaRadiusKm":40,"splitGroupEnabled":false,"maxPredicateDepth":6,"maxPredicateNodes":30,"maxRegionDepth":6,"maxRegionNodes":20}
# S51-D5 (ADR 0045 §2a, ADR 0006 §A.6): dedicated resolvePlace dimension at 10/min/session
# (apps/server/src/session/limiter.ts:52-53, apps/server/src/app-config.ts:283); the
# 10_000 value in apps/server/test/** and apps/server/src/test/support is harness-only,
# not the deployed limit. The 750/12.5 vendor bucket is a code literal
# (apps/server/src/geocode/token-bucket.ts:21-22), not an env tunable.
RATE_LIMIT_CONFIG_JSON={"searches":{"limit":20,"windowMs":60000},"fetches":{"limit":600,"windowMs":60000},"recheck":{"limit":10,"windowMs":60000},"facetCounts":{"limit":30,"windowMs":60000},"resolvePlace":{"limit":10,"windowMs":60000},"suggestPlace":{"limit":30,"windowMs":60000},"facetCountMaxCandidates":40,"concurrentSearches":3,"breachWindowMs":60000}
SESSION_COOKIE_POLICY_JSON={"sameSite":"Lax","maxAgeSeconds":86400}
# S51 (ADR 0045 §2, gate 14): Mapbox Geocoding access token is in `.env.dev.secrets` —
# requiredString, no default
# (apps/server/src/app-config.ts:135, apps/server/src/geocode/config.ts:19-20). The
# production stack supplies a real token; the dev value below is a placeholder that
# satisfies the requiredString gate without a live Mapbox call (tests inject a stub
# GeocodeResolver/fetch and never hit Mapbox). BuildAppOptions.mapboxAccessToken is
# optional-with-fallback (apps/server/src/app.ts:90, :132) only for the harness;
# production path is appConfigFromEnv requiredString -> startApp -> buildApp
# (config.mapboxAccessToken) and never bypasses the gate.
# ADR 0002 §2.3/this ADR's own allowlist convention — amc's real host, allowlisted even
PROVIDER_HOST_ALLOWLISTS_JSON={"amc":["www.amctheatres.com"]}
# Browser CORS allowlist (apps/server/src/app-config.ts) — comma-separated exact origins,
# no trailing slash, no wildcard. Required with no default (gate 14). The dev value is the
# canonical Expo web origin — the `web` service's published port below (`WEB_PORT`,
# default 8081, matching `expo start`'s own default and `apps/mobile-web/app.json`'s lack
# of a custom port). Credentials are required for cookie-based session transport
# (`credentials: 'include'` in cookieJar.ts).
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8081
# ---- web role (Expo dev server, apps/mobile-web, docker-compose.dev.yml's `web`
# service) ----
# Host-published port for the Expo web dev server. Keep this in sync with
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS above if you ever change it — the api only trusts that one origin.
WEB_PORT=8081
# ---- relay role (profiles: ["full"]) ----
RELAY_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=1000
RELAY_BATCH_SIZE=50
RELAY_RETRY_BACKOFF=5000
RELAY_ALARM_THRESHOLD_MS=60000
RELAY_HEALTH_PORT=9200

# ---- sweeper role (profiles: ["full"]) ----
SWEEP_TICK_INTERVAL_MS=5000
SWEEP_OUTBOX_BATCH=50
SWEEP_REARM_AGE=2 minutes
SWEEP_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
SWEEP_SNAPSHOT_AGE=5 minutes
SWEEP_PG_POOL_MAX=5
SWEEP_PG_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
SWEEP_PG_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000

# ---- fetch-worker (profiles: ["full"]) ----
# dispatch worker set (apps/server/src/dispatch/entry.ts). NOTE the exact var name:
# DISPATCH_PG_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS (no "POOL") — the private production templates (not shipped
# in this repo) have a pre-existing typo (`DISPATCH_PG_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS`) that the
# reader never actually consumes; flagged separately, not fixed here (out of scope).
DISPATCH_PG_POOL_MAX=5
DISPATCH_PG_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
DISPATCH_PG_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
DISPATCH_LEASE_TTL=1 minute
# catalogue-crawl tick loop (apps/server/src/catalogue-crawl/entrypoint.ts). Dev-only label,
# never rotated/used as a proxy selector (P6.15) — see catalogue-crawl/entrypoint.ts's doc
# comment. The catalogue crawler itself is not exercised by this plan's verification (it
# targets the theatre *directory*, not the seeded theatres/schedules above) but still needs
# a legal value to start without crashing (gate 14: every value required, none defaulted).
PG_POOL_MAX=5
PG_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
PG_POOL_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
AMC_USER_AGENT=SeatFirst-Dev/1.0 (local development/testing use; mailto:dev@seatfirst.example)
AMC_NAVIGATION_TIMEOUT_MS=20000
AMC_SEMAPHORE_TTL_MS=30000
# Discovered, not guessed (`dev/README.md`), by building the image and running:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml --env-file .env.dev --env-file .env.dev.secrets build fetch-worker
#   docker run --rm seatfirst-dev-fetch-worker find /ms-playwright -iname 'chrome' -type f
# Tracks the playwright-core version packages/browser-runtime/package.json pins — re-run the
# discovery command above (and update this line) if that version ever bumps.
CHROME_EXECUTABLE_PATH=/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome
AMC_CLEANUP_GRACE_PERIOD_MS=5000
AMC_READINESS_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# P6.16: "supervisor readiness probe target, never AMC" — the documented-safe local value,
# identical to what the production compose uses (its own healthcheck target).
AMC_READINESS_TARGET_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787/
AGGREGATE_PG_POOL_MAX=5
AGGREGATE_PG_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
AGGREGATE_PG_POOL_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
AGGREGATE_PROVIDER_HOST_ALLOWLISTS_JSON={"amc":["www.amctheatres.com"]}
# ADR 0023 decision 7 (real value, not a dev invention).
AGGREGATE_OFFER_STALENESS_MS=120000
RUN_PG_MAX=5
RUN_PG_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
RUN_PG_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
RUN_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS=5000
RUN_LEASE_TTL=5 minutes
RUN_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# Audit-metadata label (P6.15), never a route selector. Fixture-only mode: telemetry-only.
# `AMC_LIVE_FETCH=true` mode: this becomes the REAL attribution label attached to real AMC
# requests — keep it distinct from production's own `EGRESS_IDENTITY_LABEL` value (never
# copy that value here) so the two stacks' audit trails are never conflated. Compose-level
# isolation cannot guarantee packets actually egress under this label rather than a
# concurrently-running production Tailscale relay's route — see `docker-compose.dev.yml`'s
# header for why, and verify your actual egress IP before trusting this label.
EGRESS_IDENTITY_LABEL=seatfirst-dev-local

# ---- AMC_LIVE_FETCH (profiles: ["full"]) ----
# Decided by Josh Wu (ADR 0034, config-flag path, 2026-08-23; extended to public
# self-hosters 2026-09-17): real AMC traffic from a local machine is authorized,
# config-flag risk explicitly accepted. Default false: the fetch-worker runs fixture-only
# (`dev-entrypoint.mjs`), zero live AMC traffic, structurally enforced. Set to `true` to
# instead run the SAME real `entrypoint.mjs` production uses — real Chrome, real navigation,
# real requests to `www.amctheatres.com`, for BOTH the RUN provider-fetch actor and the
# S26/ADR-0022 catalogue-crawl loop (they share one entrypoint). Reuses production's
# request-discipline code unmodified (one-in-flight, jitter, backoff, halt-on-challenge,
# audit logging — ADR 0002 §2.3/§2.8); this flag only selects which entrypoint runs. Before
# setting this to `true`: read `dev/README.md`'s "Real AMC fetches" section and
# `docs/adr/0034-local-dev-real-amc-fetch-session-mode.md` in full (that ADR is not shipped
# in this public repo — the gist: setting this to `true` sends real requests to AMC's live
# site as you, at your own risk, and is allowed only if you first replace `AMC_USER_AGENT`'s
# shipped placeholder contact with your own real contact information), and never run it at
# the same time as another live fetch pass on the same machine (no shared semaphore between
# separate Postgres/Valkey instances — see the compose header and `dev/README.md`).
AMC_LIVE_FETCH=false

# ---- fixture-only outcome simulation (ADR 0040, profiles: ["full"]) ----
# These values apply only while AMC_LIVE_FETCH=false. The fixture fetch seam deterministically
# maps each requested showtime to one of three synthetic seat-map profiles using this seed.
# Scenario values: full (all seat fetches succeed), mixed-partial (75% succeed / 25% fail), or
# all-error (every seat fetch fails). Record both values when you reproduce a dev-stack result.
DEV_FIXTURE_SCENARIO=full
DEV_FIXTURE_SEED=seatfirst-dev-fixture-v1

# ---- seed / migrate one-shot services ----
# DATABASE_URL above covers both; DEV_FIXTURES_DIR defaults correctly inside the container
# (bind-mounted at the same repo-root-relative path the seed script/dev-entrypoint both
# compute — see dev/README.md) and does not need to be set here.

# ---- tmdb role — OPT-IN BY PRESENCE, makes REAL calls to api.themoviedb.org ----
# The ONE value in this file left genuinely blank by default rather than a working value.
# No `--profile` flag needed: the `tmdb` service is always part of the default service set
# and checks this at container startup — blank means it logs a skip message and exits
# cleanly (no crash loop); a real TMDB API key (a v4 read-access Bearer token from
# https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api) means it runs for real (ADR 0019). Leaving it
# blank costs you nothing — it enables no AMC traffic and no AMC access of any kind. The
# worker enforces its own ~30 req/s token-bucket rate cap internally, hard-coded
# (apps/server/src/tmdb/token-bucket.ts), so no other traffic/rate env is needed.
# TMDB_API_KEY is in `.env.dev.secrets`.
